  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study on Social Security Access for Migrants in Iberoamerica</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ibero-American Social Security Organization, in partnership with the Spanish Agency for International Development Cooperation, proposes to develop a study to evaluate social security access for migrants in Ibero-American countries. the objective is to contribute to improve the quantitative and qualitative access to social security systems for migrants in 22 Ibero-American countries, this analysis will include secondary data and interviews with key stakeholders in the benefiting countries. It is proposed as an outcome that specialized social security public institutions incorporate the study&apos;s recommendations in their daily practices to improve migrant&apos;s access to social security.</narrative>
  </description>
